description: Project conventions for Traceback (React/Vite/TanStack + Hono API)
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the conventions in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) — it is the canonical
instructions file for this repository.

Key points:

- Use `bun` / `bunx`, never `npm` / `npx`.
- Run `bun run verify` (lint + typecheck + format + test + build) before
  considering any change complete.
- All new features require tests (Vitest + Testing Library, co-located).
- `src/routeTree.gen.ts` is generated by TanStack Router — never edit by hand.
- Only stage files related to the current task; never force push.

Traceback-specific:

- Findings are FACT, CORRELATION, or INFERENCE. An INFERENCE must cite the
  correlations beneath it and is only ever confirmed by a human — never by the
  system.
- The LLM receives already-derived findings, never raw telemetry, and references
  them by id. Keep the id-validation gate in `server/llm.ts`: unknown ids are
  discarded before anything is written.
- Keep `server/pipeline.ts` pure — no database or network calls — so the
  correlation rules stay unit-testable.
- Missing integrations must degrade, not break, and every fallback must be
  labelled as one in the response and the UI.
- Secrets are server-side only. Never give a secret a `VITE_` prefix: Vite
  inlines those into the browser bundle.
- Put colours in `src/index.css` as tokens, not hardcoded Tailwind palette
  classes in components.
